            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This is real UX issue:  rebooting the BMC is a \u201cwait and wonder\u201d moment.\nThe three-step firmware-switch messaging is a nice touch.\n\nIt needs a little polish on the \u201chow do we know it\u2019s really back?\u201d logic."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 392,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "i18n gap: Only en-US updated for the new step toasts; ka-GE / ru-RU still have old keys."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 392,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "+1, Need to change in other languages as well"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/GlobalStore.js",
                    "line": 152,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Hardcoded `/redfish/v1/Systems/system` \u2014 use existing `getSystemPath()`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/GlobalStore.js",
                    "line": 155,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Stores only `LastState`\ncallers use if (this.bootProgress) which is true for `\"None\"` and pre-reboot `\"OSRunning\"`, so completion can fire on the first poll while BMC is still up.\n\nSuggest storing `{ PowerState, BootProgress }` and gating completion on stable state: `PowerState === 'On'` and `LastState in ('None', 'OSRunning')`, with a minimum wait after BMC becomes reachable again (BMCs often report On + None before boot firmware updates progress)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/GlobalStore.js",
                    "line": 156,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "No optional chaining on `data.BootProgress.LastState`\nthrows if BootProgress is absent."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/Firmware/FirmwareCardsBmc.vue",
                    "line": 137,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "`isReadonly` is undefined.\n\npass as prop from parent?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/Firmware/FirmwareCardsBmc.vue",
                    "line": 178,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "same issue as in RebootBmc.vue. (a false positive)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/Firmware/FirmwareCardsBmc.vue",
                    "line": 192,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Missing \u2014 cleanup: No timer cancellation on navigation away."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/Firmware/FirmwareCardsBmc.vue",
                    "line": 202,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Concern: Arbitrary 120s setTimeout in step3() after detection \u2014 document rationale or replace with stable-state detection."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/RebootBmc/RebootBmc.vue",
                    "line": 87,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "`rebootBmc()` and `checkBmcRebootCompletion()` both call startLoader(), so it is called twice."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/RebootBmc/RebootBmc.vue",
                    "line": 105,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "wrong error on timeout: When `checkCounter > 10`, `this.errorToast(message)` passes the success start string from the dispatch, not an error. \n\nUse `pageRebootBmc.toast.errorRebootStart` or a dedicated timeout key."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/RebootBmc/RebootBmc.vue",
                    "line": 108,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "For BMC-only reboot, does ComputerSystem.BootProgress actually change? If not, consider polling Manager `Status.State === 'Enabled'` or `/redfish/v1` reachability instead.\n\nIn fact, consider polling `/redfish/v1` until it responds\nThen poll Manager `Status.State === 'Enabled'`\n*Then* poll `ComputerSystem.BootProgress`\n\nAnd consider putting this in a composable instead of in a .vue file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/RebootBmc/RebootBmc.vue",
                    "line": 109,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "treats any truthy LastState as \u201creboot complete,\u201d including values already present before reboot. Need unreachable \u2192 reachable \u2192 stable-state sequence."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Operations/RebootBmc/RebootBmc.vue",
                    "line": 117,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Recursive setTimeout polling continues after route leave (up to ~10 min). Cancel in beforeRouteLeave / beforeUnmount."
                }
            ],
